  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "USB",
      "items": [
        "scripts/usb.sh: adb reverse tcp:8790 tcp:8790, then opens the page on the phone; with a certificate the edge speaks https there too (usb.sh 10–17).",
        "opened() calls a link from a loopback address \"usb\", any other \"wifi\"; the hello event says which (core.py 103–105)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Wi-Fi by QR",
      "items": [
        "./start.sh --make-cert makes certs/: an authority (its key never leaves the PC) and the edge's certificate for this PC's addresses (make_cert.sh 5–13, start.sh 118–123).",
        "The setup page draws the QR of /ca.crt and of the page (setup.js 116–118). /ws then needs the same Origin and, with --key, the key (wsserver.py 368–373)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "One phone",
      "items": [
        "take_over() waits for a message being delivered, swaps the link, closes the old one with 4000; app.html does not reconnect after 4000 (wsserver.py 265–277, app.js 217–220).",
        "Before 23b2ca7 a backend that stopped reading kept that lock: diagram 07."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
